753	    /// Moves the clip's end edge to `to`, clamped to the source's remaining
754	    /// length (media sources) and to at least one frame of clip (spec §6).
755	    /// The source in point and the actions are untouched. The bound is
756	    /// `source_window.rs`'s `latest_end_on_grid`, measured at this clip's
757	    /// OWN start: the last frame at or before the end of the file, and
758	    /// never the one past it (spec §11, #22 and D4-2). A ramped clip's bound
759	    /// reads its map on past the end (S∞, spec §11 SR-18 (a)). A graphic's
760	    /// `length` is untouched: null follows the new end, a number stays (G-9).
761	    /// `alone` is `trim_start`'s: without it a linked partner ending where
762	    /// this clip ends follows; with it, the L-cut (spec §11 AU-93).
763	    pub fn trim_end(&self, clip: u32, to: Ticks, alone: bool) -> Result<Outcome, String> {
764	        self.carried_edge(
765	            clip,
766	            alone,
767	            |target, partner| clip_end(partner) == clip_end(target),
768	            |project, id| project.trim_end_one(id, to),
769	        )
770	    }
